@i_alpha:I{ky=~2:al;pr=@project;so=[@s_refobs];st=observed;vl=binary;wh=@user;wy=~132:Both references contain zero fractional-alpha pixels. Observed from the source art; not yet confirmed as this project output policy.}
@i_animation:I{ky=~9:animation;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~456:The brief names a character family but states no poses, cycles, directions or timing, and neither reference shows motion; both retained sources name this gap. The saved plan treats the sample, scout and medic as single static side-view sprites. Not needed for the representative sample. Before scout/medic production it decides whether each output is one sprite or an animation set, which changes the planned output kinds and the PixelLab operation to use.}
@i_backgrounds:I{ky=~18:target_backgrounds;pr=@project;so=[@s_continuation];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~372:The predominant level backgrounds of the side-view game are not stated. The retained comparison sheet showed the navy outline separates the figure on busy mid-value backgrounds but nearly disappears on dark ones, so the outline decision depends on this. The light, dark and busy bands used in the readability criterion are the agent's test set, not the game's backgrounds.}
@i_canvas:I{ky=~2:px;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs,@s_eval_answers];st=proposed;vl=[32,32];wh=@user;wy=~888:Status moved unresolved -> proposed in revision 9 on the authority of sources/controlled-evaluation-answers.md (s_eval_answers): 32 x 32 is confirmed for the representative sample only, with the stated limits that it is not a real owner preference, does not bind family or production policy and is not human acceptance. `proposed` rather than `confirmed` because the owner has explicitly not chosen the final canvas size (s_brief) and the input does not change that; a confirmed status would read as the project canvas and would clear the production-phase unconfirmed gate once a production contract links this choice. 32 x 32 is also the measured canvas of both references carrying an 18 x 25 figure (s_refobs), an observation that did not by itself adopt the value. Supplies C.px of the sample contract c_sample. The final canvas for scout/medic production remains the owner's decision.}
@i_design_language:I{ky=~15:design_language;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs];st=proposed;vl=~257:Carry the flat colour, absent anti-aliasing, binary alpha and blocky low-detail construction of the references into a genuinely side-view figure; treat the front-facing symmetric shape of the references as a style swatch rather than as the character design.;wh=@user;wy=~295:Proposal needing the agreement of the owner. Both references are front-facing and bilaterally symmetric while the stated destination is a side-view game, so the reference pose cannot be reproduced literally. This proposal states which parts of the references are being matched and which are not.}
@i_display_scale:I{ky=~13:display_scale;pr=@project;so=[@s_methods];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~224:The target on-screen integer zoom is not stated. The bundled integer-presentation method requires a target viewport as an input, and the scale bounds how much interior detail survives, so it interacts with the canvas choice.}
@i_engine:I{ky=~6:engine;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~112:No destination engine or importer is named, so no engine import acceptance can be performed in this project yet.}
@i_lighting:I{ky=~8:lighting;pr=@project;so=[@s_refobs,@s_ref_a,@s_ref_b];st=observed;vl=~45:flat (no directional light, no shading ramps);wh=@user;wy=~647:Measured from the references: three flat colours in reference.png and two in reference-b.png, each a single flat value with no ramp, no anti-aliasing and no directional shading. This observation supplies the lighting component of the sample contract's li field, which the kit defines as lighting and aesthetic intent; li is composed at contract time from this choice, the design-language proposal and the outline answer. Keyed `lighting` rather than `li` so linking it through C.ch does not pin the whole intent string to the lighting phrase (corrected from revision 7). Observed from the source art; not confirmed as this project's output policy.}
@i_outline:I{ky=~14:edge_treatment;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs,@s_ref_a,@s_ref_b,@s_eval_answers];st=proposed;vl=~132:reference.png: flat 2px dark outline #25354A fully enclosing the body, also carrying the shoulder bar, base bar and solid top stalks;wh=@user;wy=~1297:Status moved conflict -> proposed in revision 9 on the authority of sources/controlled-evaluation-answers.md (s_eval_answers), which confirms the outlined treatment of reference.png for the representative sample only and states that it does not express a real owner preference, bind family or production policy, or provide human acceptance. `proposed` rather than `confirmed`: the project-level choice remains the owner's; a confirmed status would present a sample-scoped evaluation answer as an owner decision and would clear the production-phase unconfirmed gate once a production contract links this choice. The value is the first of the two alternatives retained while this choice was in conflict; the other alternative remains open for the family and for production: 'reference-b.png: no outline, flat teal silhouette with cream eyes only'. Measured context unchanged: the two references differ in exactly 180 pixels, every one #25354A becoming #56B5BC; the outline is load-bearing rather than trim because it also carries the shoulder bar, base bar and stalk interiors; the bundled edge-rhythm method states contour style is authored intent and must not be resolved mechanically. The owner's own answer, informed by deliverables/outline-decision-brief.md, still decides the family treatment.}
@i_palette:I{ky=~2:pl;pr=@project;so=[@s_refobs,@s_ref_a,@s_ref_b,@s_eval_answers];st=observed;vl=[~7:#56B5BC,~7:#F4DDA2,~7:#25354A];wh=@user;wy=~738:Measured from the references: teal body #56B5BC and cream eyes #F4DDA2 in both, navy #25354A present only in reference.png. Observed, not agreed. Revision 9: the sample-scoped outlined-treatment answer in sources/controlled-evaluation-answers.md (s_eval_answers) brings #25354A into the sample's working palette, so all three measured colours supply C.pl of c_sample; the status stays observed because no owner instruction has adopted these exact values as the project palette and the answer binds the sample only. Confirmation for production remains coupled to the unresolved role-differentiation device (i_role_diff), which may need a reserved accent; the exclusive membership rule in q_palette is a derived rule, not a brief statement.}
@i_role_diff:I{ky=~20:role_differentiation;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~271:How a scout reads as a scout and a medic as a medic is not stated, and neither reference carries role-identifying equipment or accent colour. At the detail density of the references this needs a deliberate device, such as a reserved accent hue or a silhouette attachment.}
@i_roster:I{ky=~6:roster;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief];st=confirmed;vl=[~5:scout,~5:medic];wh=@user;wy=~49:The brief names exactly these two family members.}
@i_sampling:I{ky=~2:sa;pr=@project;so=[@s_methods];st=proposed;vl=nearest;wh=@user;wy=~194:Proposal. Neither reference contains anti-aliasing or dithering, so nearest sampling preserves the supplied look. Proposed rather than confirmed because the display scale and engine are unknown.}
@i_view:I{ky=~2:vw;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief];st=confirmed;vl=side;wh=@user;wy=~53:The brief states the destination is a side-view game.}
@project:P{br=~271:Character family matching the supplied references for a side-view game: a scout and a medic. The two supplied references disagree about outline treatment, and the user has not chosen the final canvas size. Begin the project and make the progress possible in this session.;in=[@i_outline,@i_canvas,@i_display_scale,@i_view,@i_roster,@i_palette,@i_alpha,@i_sampling,@i_design_language,@i_role_diff,@i_engine,@i_backgrounds,@i_lighting,@i_animation];nm=~32:Scout and Medic character family;ow=@user;sc=[@s_brief,@s_refobs,@s_methods,@s_ref_a,@s_ref_b]}
@q_aid_faithful:Q{ck=~261:Every enlarged sprite panel in the sheet is an exact integer nearest-neighbour enlargement of the supplied reference bytes: each source pixel becomes a uniform z-by-z block of the identical colour, and no sprite pixel takes a colour absent from its source file.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~38:decision aid is a faithful enlargement;so=[@s_methods];wh=@user}
@q_aid_useful:Q{ck=~215:Viewed as an image, the sheet shows both outline treatments together at every sampled display scale on light, dark and busy backgrounds, and the difference between them is visible well enough to choose between them.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~34:decision aid supports the decision;so=[@s_refobs];wh=@user}
@q_canvas:Q{ck=~136:The candidate file matches the confirmed canvas size exactly and contains zero fractional-alpha pixels under the confirmed alpha policy.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~16:canvas and alpha;so=[@s_brief];wh=@user}
@q_engine_import:Q{ck=~159:The destination engine imports the sprites with the intended nearest sampling, integer scale, pivot placement and transparency, verified in the running engine.;dm=engine;md=live;nm=~25:destination engine import;so=[@s_brief];wh=@user}
@q_family_continuity:Q{ck=~138:Viewed together at equal zoom the family members share height, volume, eye-line, ground contact and anchor placement, and use one palette.;dm=continuity;md=visual;nm=~17:family continuity;so=[@s_brief];wh=@user}
@q_outline:Q{ck=~195:The candidate applies the confirmed outline treatment consistently on every contour and on the interior landmarks that treatment is responsible for, inspected at native scale and at integer zoom.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~25:outline treatment applied;so=[@s_refobs];wh=@user}
@q_palette:Q{ck=~110:Every visible pixel of the candidate is a member of the confirmed project palette, with no colours outside it.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~18:palette membership;so=[@s_refobs];wh=@user}
@q_readability:Q{ck=~176:At native scale on light, dark and busy backgrounds the figure reads as a side-view character with an unambiguous facing direction and separable head, torso and limb landmarks.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~21:side-view readability;so=[@s_methods];wh=@user}
@q_role_read:Q{ck=~115:At native scale a viewer can tell the scout from the medic by silhouette or accent alone, without text or a legend.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~35:scout and medic are distinguishable;so=[@s_brief];wh=@user}
@q_sample_canvas:Q{ck=~364:The candidate file is exactly 32 x 32 pixels, the canvas of the sample contract c_sample, and contains zero fractional-alpha pixels under that contract's binary alpha. Scope: the representative sample only; the canvas is a sample-scoped controlled-evaluation confirmation and the alpha policy an observation from the references, neither a confirmed project policy.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~23:sample canvas and alpha;so=[@s_eval_answers,@s_refobs];wh=@actor}
@q_sample_outline:Q{ck=~569:Inspected at native scale and at integer zoom, the candidate applies the outlined treatment of the sample contract c_sample, the treatment shown in reference.png: a flat #25354A contour at the weight shown there (2 logical px) fully enclosing the figure, applied consistently on every contour and also carrying the interior landmarks that treatment is responsible for (shoulder bar, base bar, solid top stalks) adapted to the side view. Scope: the representative sample only, under the sample-scoped controlled-evaluation confirmation; not a confirmed family treatment.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~32:sample outline treatment applied;so=[@s_eval_answers,@s_ref_a,@s_refobs];wh=@actor}
@q_sample_palette:Q{ck=~444:Every visible pixel of the candidate is one of the three colours of the sample contract c_sample palette, #56B5BC, #F4DDA2 and #25354A, with no colours outside it. Scope: the representative sample only; these are the colours measured in the references, all three admitted by the sample-scoped outlined-treatment confirmation, and exclusivity is a sample working rule that a later role accent may reopen; this is not a confirmed project palette.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~25:sample palette membership;so=[@s_refobs,@s_eval_answers];wh=@actor}
@q_sample_readability:Q{ck=~510:At native scale and at the target integer zoom, on light, dark and busy test backgrounds, the figure reads as a side-view character with an unambiguous facing direction, and the identity landmarks named in the sample contract c_sample (two notched top stalks, cream eye placement, navy shoulder bar, navy base bar, enclosing navy contour) remain separable. The target integer zoom requires i_display_scale before review; the three test backgrounds are the specialist's test set until i_backgrounds is answered.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~28:sample side-view readability;so=[@s_methods,@s_refobs,@s_continuation_2];wh=@actor}
@q_study_complete:Q{ck=~176:The retained study states both reference file identities by hash, the exact count and nature of the pixel differences between them, and names every choice it leaves unresolved.;dm=other;md=local;nm=~24:reference study complete;so=[@s_brief];wh=@user}
@q_study_seen:Q{ck=~182:Both references were actually inspected at native scale and at integer enlargement, and the description in the study of the outline treatment and eye placement matches what was seen.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~39:reference study matches what was viewed;so=[@s_refobs];wh=@user}
@q_style_match:Q{ck=~157:Viewed beside reference.png and reference-b.png at equal integer zoom, the candidate reads as the same art style in colour, detail density and edge language.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~23:reads as the same style;so=[@s_refobs];wh=@user}
